cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite the dataset itself."
type: dataset
title: "MCP Parameter-Description Ablation: Null-Result Experiment Dataset"
authors:
  - family-names: Clouâtre
    given-names: Hugues
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4291-1999"
repository-code: "https://github.com/clouatre-labs/param-description-experiments"
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-09-19"
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >
  Supplementary dataset for a pre-registered ablation experiment testing whether moving
  parameter-level detail out of an MCP tool's description string and into
  inputSchema.properties[*].description regresses parameter-filling accuracy, especially
  for smaller models. Contains two experiments: exp1-analyze-symbol, a 320-call run across
  two models in a 2x2 cell design, blind-scored at two scoring resolutions, with no
  significant parameter-filling difference (Mann-Whitney U, n=40/cell) but a significant
  input-token reduction for the lean description; and exp2-response-format, a collapse A/B
  of response-shaping parameters into a single response_format enum, also null on
  parameter-filling with a small significant token saving. Includes fixtures, prompts,
  rubrics, raw call transcripts, blind scores, and pre-registered protocols locked before
  scoring.
keywords:
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp
  - llm-evaluation
  - tool-use
  - function-calling
  - ablation-study
  - null-result
  - pre-registered
  - mann-whitney-u
  - prompt-engineering
  - input-schema
  - agentic-ai
